{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/549979-momentum-for-persistant-legend","id":549979,"title":"Momentum for Persistant Legend.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-11T05:36:24-07:00","id":549979,"title":"Momentum for Persistant Legend.","content":"A Demon player on a game I'm running wants to use the Momentum Embed to boost his Cover roll to achieve Legend and then apply the Persisitant Legend Embed on it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I want to allow this. We have a bigger than average playerbase (we're online, not tabletop) and I don't know if I want to set this precedent. Do you guys have any advice regarding why I should allow it regardless (maybe I'm being paranoid) or why you think thematically or mechanically it shouldn't be allowed?<br /> <br /> Thanks. I appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T06:11:52-07:00","id":550041,"title":"","content":"Well... I don't see why it shouldn't. A number of players have fun trying to find ways to mix and match abilities, and there's a lot stranger combinations out there that will have an issue. Adding in the Momentum Embed doesn't do anything other than increase your dice pool - its not actually making anything too much better other than having a nice die pool and a lucky roll. In this one case, using Momentum should be fine. The precedent you are talking about, however, I think is abuse of constantly using this for everyone, and everything. <br /> <br /> One thing that I've picked up from what the writers have said on here, but isn't really detailed in the book, is that continual repeatedly using an Embed can cause Compromise checks. If you're familiar with Mage, then you should be aware of how subtle magic can become improbable. Demon Embeds work in a similar way - if you use them in a way that's not subtle, the God-Machine picks up on it, and it causes a Compromise check. If you consistently use the same Embed combination over and over (like Momentum into Just Bruised over and over), no one is that lucky, and again, it raises the God-Machine's notice. <br /> <br /> So that tends to be the limiting factor for things. If someone starts abusing a power, call for Compromise checks. Its really amazing how that sharply curves abuse when players realize that such abuse can degrade their Cover. <br /> <br /> Another limiting factor with Momentum is that, from my reading of the embed, you're actually declaring to use the power before the roll is made, and he can see the successes. So, the player would have no idea on what he'd get for bonus dice, and could actually only get one extra die (big deal) or no dice. If he doesn't like the roll he gets, and wants to drop it and reroll? Remember that subsequent rolls, as per WoD rules, suffer a cumulative -1 penalty, especially the Imposter Condition. <br /> <br /> I'd also rule that you cannot maintain a Legend when switching between Covers - so, switching to a new Cover is the same as choosing to disable Legend. And sticking with one Cover can go badly fast - its too easy to act out of Cover.<br /> <br /> <br /> Between all the above, you can see where there would be serious checks on your player's current plan from being abused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:47:51-07:00","id":551351,"title":"","content":"Thanks, MCN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:43:24-07:00","id":556525,"title":"","content":"I think a good rule of thumb for 'abuse' of embeds is the old detective story trope: &quot;Once is random chance, Twice is a freak accident, Thrice is a pattern&quot;.<br /> <br /> Going back into the cold war/spycraft thing - if your players are getting predictable in how they continuously use their embeds (especially in this fashion), that's probably a good time to rule compromises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T05:17:00-07:00","id":556771,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Xenesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}